<item>
  <title>2026-05-12 Thresholds in Clinical Practice</title>
  <dc:creator>Events </dc:creator>
  <link>https://drganghe.github.io/quarto-academic-website-template/posts/event-title/event1.html</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<section id="summary-of-meeting-topics" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="summary-of-meeting-topics">Summary of meeting topics</h2>
<ul>
<li>Scores and GEMS (Global Examination of Mental State) ability to identify pathologies</li>
<li>Two types of cut-offs: Clinical (e.g.&nbsp;Crawford &amp; Grathwaite, 1998, 2006) and ROC. Advantages, disadvantages, and does it make sense to have both?</li>
<li>Correspondence between cognitive domains and tasks (i.e.&nbsp;on validity and measurement error).</li>
</ul>
